=== H2d exact member name 'syn-ref' also a prefix of 'syn-refusal' (leak must not happen) ===
$ python3 census-probe.py --waive syn-ref
pass [A] syn-pass
refused [A] syn-ref: fail-closed refusal: synthetic missing dependency (marker 'missing dependency') [waived]
refused [A] syn-refusal: fail-closed refusal: synthetic missing dependency (marker 'missing dependency')
HOST_CENSUS pass=1 fail=0 not_evaluated=2 waived=1 total=3 tierA_fail=0 tierB_fail=0
CENSUS_NOT_EVALUATED 1 member(s) without a waiver: syn-refusal — exit 1
[exit] 1

=== H2e space-named member, prefix only ===
$ python3 census-probe.py --waive test-snapshot
pass [A] syn-pass
refused [A] test-snapshot harness: fail-closed refusal: synthetic missing dependency (marker 'missing dependency')
HOST_CENSUS pass=1 fail=0 not_evaluated=1 total=2 tierA_fail=0 tierB_fail=0
CENSUS_NOT_EVALUATED 1 member(s) without a waiver: test-snapshot harness — exit 1
[stderr] warning: --waive 'test-snapshot' is not a census member name
[exit] 1

=== H2f space-named member, exact quoted name ===
$ python3 census-probe.py --waive test-snapshot harness
pass [A] syn-pass
refused [A] test-snapshot harness: fail-closed refusal: synthetic missing dependency (marker 'missing dependency') [waived]
HOST_CENSUS pass=1 fail=0 not_evaluated=1 waived=1 total=2 tierA_fail=0 tierB_fail=0
[exit] 0

=== H2g space-named member, equals form ===
$ python3 census-probe.py --waive=test-snapshot harness
pass [A] syn-pass
refused [A] test-snapshot harness: fail-closed refusal: synthetic missing dependency (marker 'missing dependency') [waived]
HOST_CENSUS pass=1 fail=0 not_evaluated=1 waived=1 total=2 tierA_fail=0 tierB_fail=0
[exit] 0

